WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.367
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-, Grammy-,

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:06.334
Tony- and Academy Award-winning
actress, singer and producer,

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:07.901
and the host of
"The Jennifer Hudson Show,"

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:10.067
which airs every weekday.
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:12.100
our friend Jennifer Hudson,
everybody.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:21.200
♪♪

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:29.067
♪♪

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.534
Hello. Welcome back.
-Whoo!

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.133
[ Cheers and applause continue ]
-So happy you're here.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.300
-Thank you.
I'm happy to be here.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.634
-I think we're still
technically within the window

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:40.601
where I can talk
about Halloween costumes.

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:42.701
Do you agree?
-Yeah, a little bit.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:46.267
-I mostly just want to talk
about you dressed up

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.734
like Missy Elliott
on your show

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:50.267
from the famous
"The Rain" video, right?

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:53.200
-Yes, I did.
-That's Missy. And you...

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.734
There was no -- I mean,
no shortcuts here.

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.634
-No, we go all the way.
-You went all the way.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.200
This is not some last-minute

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.801
"I'm going to be Missy Elliott
going to a Halloween party."

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.334
Like, throwing a Hefty bag on
or something.

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:06.934
-No.
-You just went the whole look.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.701
-The whole look. Yes, I did.
-And she saw it.

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:10.734
-Yes, she did.

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.133
-And she liked it.
-She loved it.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:16.534
-And she wrote, "You merked dat.
Whooty whoo.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.734
You won. I love you."
-That meant something good.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.234
-That's something good.
-It did.

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:24.467
It came from Missy.
-I'll tell you this.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.234
I'm starting to come
to the conclusion that no one's

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:27.834
ever going to tell me
I merked anything.

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.167
[ Laughter ]
-I don't know. If you dress --

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.167
-You're never too late to merk.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:34.634
We've talked
about artists that inspired you.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.334
Like Aretha last time
you were here.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.801
But Missy was someone
who inspired you

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.467
when you were younger.
-Oh, my God, yes.

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.434
I mean, Missy is a legend.
-She is a legend.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.067
-So I had to sneak it in there,
you know, like,

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.400
pay homage to her
with my Halloween costume.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.100
So I really thought I was her
in the moment.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.100
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.534
-I bet she's a very fun person

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.868
to think you are for a moment.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.267
-She is a fun person,
that's for sure.

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:56.868
And somebody, you know,
to pay homage to.

00:01:56.868 --> 00:01:58.634
-It's really -- I mean,
it is a nice thing

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.467
that I think happens where
all of a sudden you realize,

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.033
like someone, you know,

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:04.934
you listened to when you were
younger is now a legend.

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:07.734
You know, you were
like someone you were aware of

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.167
and your parents weren't.
-Right.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.234
-And then all of a sudden
you're like,

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.701
"Oh, and now they are just
a legend."

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.734
-Yes. And my kid wasn't aware

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:16.133
because he came with me
to work that day

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:18.834
when we -- I was in my Missyness
and he was like, "Who is that?"

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.968
He's like, "Oh, Mama, you ain't
going to be able to do that."

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.000
But I did it
and I pulled it off.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.434
-I can't believe you --
-You see my Missy skills, kid?

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:26.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:31.200
-I can't believe your son
doesn't think you can do it.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.767
-No. You know how kids are.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.334
They don't think you can do
anything.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:37.567
-Now, one thing you've done
since the last time you're here,

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:38.801
you were about to start
your talk show,

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.567
and now you're
in your second season.

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:44.300
Six Emmy nominations,
including best talk show.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.968
-How am I doing? Thank you.
-You're a natural.

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:48.000
-Thank you.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.334
-You were saying
one of the interesting --

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:50.667
We were talking backstage that
now

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:52.434
that you actually have
your own talk show,

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:54.200
you realize when you're a guest
on a talk show

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.067
that everybody who in the past
just seemed

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.067
like they were running around,
they all serve a purpose.

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.434
-Yes. You know,
now I get to understand.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:01.767
Yeah. Why all the people
running around,

00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:02.934
what they doing,
who's talking to me,

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:04.834
what am I supposed to do
when I come out here,

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.434
you know, the whole field
because it's different now

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.601
being on the other side
as the host.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.234
And then it's weird again,
though,

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.834
but cool being the guest.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.467
I'm still trying
to make sense out of it.

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:18.434
-Yeah. Did you -- Was there
a part of hosting a show

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:21.434
that you were most worried
about before you kicked it off?

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.767
-You know what?

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.968
Speaking publicly, it's like
one of my biggest fears.

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.834
-Oh.
-So to take it on and like,

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.300
"Oh, you want me to talk
to a whole audience?"

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.367
And the first, like --
when we first started the show,

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.734
we would go like in for prep,

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:36.868
and if I was singing,
then I would do a rehearsal

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.534
with the band
and then go and perform.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:40.400
If I was acting,
you work with an acting coach

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.701
and then you shoot a scene.

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:44.367
With the talk show life,
I'm like, "So we're just going

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.100
to like, sit and keep talking?"

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:50.901
"Oh! That's what this is."
So that was surprising to me.

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:52.367
-It's so funny. I would say,

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.467
of every fear,
a fear of public speaking,

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.334
I would have guessed would be
a deal breaker for this job.

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.234
-You would think but, you know.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:03.634
-It's like, "Well, I freeze up
if I see camera or lights,

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:07.000
but other than that,
I'd love to take the job."

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.467
You seem very natural.

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:10.200
And I mean, again,
one of the coolest things

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.234
about the job for me

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:13.100
is the people
you get to talk to

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.501
that you feel like maybe
you never would have

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:15.868
had a conversation
with otherwise.

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:17.534
Is there anybody where
you've been talking to them

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.467
and thinking, "I can't believe
I'm here right now"?

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:22.667
-Oh, my God. Several people.
Like, I fan out on a lot.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:25.801
Like, I got to sit
with Smokey Robinson.

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:28.133
-That's a pretty good one.
-Talked to him.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:29.567
And sometimes
I want to scream like,

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:32.000
"Oh, my God, this is Smokey
sitting right here."

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.067
But then I'd be like,
"Ooh, let me be Mrs. Host."

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.367
Like, whatever that is
to keep my composure.

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.400
-It is a funny thing
when you talk to legends

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.434
because you do want to do that.
You do want to scream it,

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:43.934
but you realize
they don't want to hear it

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:46.000
because they also -- he knows
he's Smokey Robinson, you know?

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:48.334
He wasn't taking
advantage of the moment.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:50.300
So the weirdest thing
is how you actually

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.667
have to, like, pump the brakes
a little bit

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.234
on your own fandom for people.
-Right.

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:56.834
To, you know,
be a host like yourself

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:59.634
and try to be polished
and, you know,

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:01.534
and not lose it and fan out.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.801
But that's who you want.
You know?

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:05.601
-Just try to always move
like a video game character.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:08.334
-Welcome to "The
Jennifer Hudson Show," you know.

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:10.534
-Yeah.
-How that's supposed to sound.

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:12.067
-It's nice when they put
your name in the title.

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:14.801
It makes it easier to remember.
Yeah, I love that.

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.367
I love that it's "Late Night
with Seth Meyers."

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.334
I'm like, "I'll forget a lot of
stuff, but that I can get."

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.634
Yeah. I have a lot more
to ask you.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:21.934
Will you stick around?
-Yes, I will.

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:24.133
-We'll be right back
with more Jennifer after this.

